---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Accessibility" description="Accessibility statement for the North Kitsap United website." heroTitle="Accessibility">
  <section class="card">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="text-sm text-nku-gray-light">Effective Date: November 17, 2026</p>

        <p>The Rotary Club of Kingston-North Kitsap is committed to improving access for visitors, including people who use assistive technologies.</p>
        <h2>Our Accessibility Approach</h2>
        <p>We use the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 Level AA as an aspirational guide for ongoing improvement. Accessibility is an evolving effort, not a representation that every page, document, form, video, map, third-party tool, or feature will satisfy every guideline at all times. Content changes, legacy files, volunteer-created materials, and third-party services may present limitations.</p>
        <h2>Ongoing Practices</h2>
        <p>We are committed to ongoing efforts to improve accessibility, which may include:</p>
        <ul>
        <li>Reviewing website content and structure</li>
        <li>use of meaningful headings, labels, link text, page titles, and navigation;</li>
        <li>support keyboard access and visible focus where the site platform permits;</li>
        <li>considerations in color contrast, text resizing, readability, captions, transcripts, and alternative text;</li>
        <li>review forms for instructions, errors, labels, and accessible completion;</li>
        <li>reviewing images and media for accessible alternatives where feasible;</li>
        <li>consider accessibility when procuring or embedding new tools, donation pages, documents, maps, or media;</li>
        <li>provide reasonable assistance or an alternate format when practical; and</li>
        <li>prioritize reported barriers based on impact, feasibility, available resources, and control over the affected content.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Third-Party and Downloadable Content</h2>
        <p>Some content and functions are provided by third parties, including Zeffy donation pages, Stripe payment processing, embedded videos, maps, social-media content, documents, or form and analytics providers. We may not control their accessibility. We will consider accessibility when selecting and configuring services and may offer a reasonable alternative where practical, but we cannot warrant a third party’s conformance or continued availability.</p>
        <h2>Feedback and Assistance</h2>
        <p>If you have difficulty using the website, identify a barrier, or need information in another format, email <a href="mailto:nku@rotaryknk.org">nku@rotaryknk.org</a>. Please identify the page or feature, describe the issue, state the format or assistance requested, and, if useful, identify the device, browser, and assistive technology. Please do not include sensitive medical or disability information unless necessary. We will review requests in good faith and respond within a reasonable time based on complexity, resources, and third-party involvement. This process is not an emergency service.</p>
        <p>We welcome feedback and use it to support ongoing improvement. No statement here waives any defense, limitation, exemption, or right available under applicable law, and no statement should be read as an admission that a particular law applies.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
